It is late afternoon, and it is still raining.
I go into the museum café and wait there.
A friendly man stands at the till.
"What can I do for you?", he asks me.
"I will take a tea and this bread roll, please," I say and point to the display.
"Gladly."
"That is four euros, please."
I pay and take my plate and my cup.
I sit down at a table directly by the large glass windows.
I eat the bread roll and look outside at the rain.
Half a year ago, my life was completely different.
Six months ago, I packed my whole life in Mexico into boxes.
I was very overwhelmed back then.
But this afternoon is wonderfully quiet.
This rain does not bother me at all.
I drink my tea in peace.
This city feels like my real home now.
I am simply happy that I am here.
